From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:09:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Popups on Windows 10 Mobile: arrow panels slide along the
 screen

The phone's theme (mobile-config-firefox) makes every panel as wide as the
screen. With panel.js's default flip="both", a panel opened from an icon in
the middle of the address bar was cut down to the room right of the icon and
ran a few pixels past the screen's edge: the microphone prompt lost its
bottom-right corner, where Allow is. On Wayland, which the theme is made for,
the compositor moves such a popup back on screen. Under GECKO_W10M an arrow
panel flipped "both" slides instead; vertical flipping is unchanged.

Done here rather than by setting the attribute from the autoconfig script:
some panels (form validation, date and colour pickers) are put in and opened
in one go, before a script could change them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
index bb9a0a491b..575c2ba35f 100644
--- a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
+++ b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
@@ -799,6 +799,19 @@ static FlipType FlipFromAttribute(nsMenuPopupFrame* aFrame) {
     return FlipType::None;
   }
   if (flip.EqualsLiteral("both")) {
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+    // The phone's theme (mobile-config-firefox) makes every panel as wide as
+    // the screen. Flipped "both", which panel.js gives every arrow panel, one
+    // opened from an icon mid-way along the address bar was cut down to the
+    // room right of the icon and ran past the screen's edge: the microphone
+    // prompt lost its bottom-right corner, where Allow is. On Wayland, which
+    // the theme is made for, the compositor moves such a popup back on
+    // screen; here an arrow panel slides along the screen instead.
+    if (aFrame->PopupElement().AttrValueIs(kNameSpaceID_None, nsGkAtoms::type,
+                                           nsGkAtoms::arrow, eCaseMatters)) {
+      return FlipType::Slide;
+    }
+#endif
     return FlipType::Both;
   }
   if (flip.EqualsLiteral("slide")) {
